{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "gpt-6-sol",
  "run": 1,
  "simulation_id": "sim-03",
  "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B001",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and development of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B011",
    "B062"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B001 remains the most secure combination of a distinctive physical idea, demanding experimental realization, maturity, and bounded individual credit. Katori's magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept made it possible to interrogate many trapped atoms without the usual motion-related frequency shifts, while Ye's foundational experimental development established the platform at the performance and reliability needed to open a new precision-measurement regime. Independent demonstrations, fundamental tests, and relativistic geodesy show that this is not a prospective application but a mature capability that enables measurements previously inaccessible. The citation should remain confined to optical lattice clocks, rather than claim all later optical-clock advances or a future redefinition of the second.",
    "case_against": "The field is extensive, and a documentary review must establish that the proposed pair fairly captures the original lattice-clock concept and its foundational development without absorbing decisive contributions by the wider optical-clock community. Its ultimate role in formal timekeeping standards remains unsettled, but that is not necessary to the present case: the experimentally verified lattice-clock achievement is already complete enough to assess.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson prefers B011 because squeezed light turns quantum fluctuations from a measurement limitation into an operational resource, while acknowledging that experimental credit is distributed across a broad lineage.",
        "response": "I continue to regard B011 as the strongest alternative. Its conceptual and practical importance for precision measurement is undeniable. But the unresolved choice among pioneering squeezing sources, loss-control work, interferometric implementation, and deployment is consequential for a three-person award. B001 has a comparably deep metrological consequence with a more compact and historically intelligible division between the lattice-clock idea and its decisive experimental development."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "olsson-eva",
        "point": "Olsson argues that B062 is a completed observational invention that transformed electron microscopy into an atomic-scale quantitative probe, while requiring careful separation of conceptual, engineering, and commercial contributions.",
        "response": "I agree that B062 exemplifies the value of an instrument that opens a new observational door and that its physical impact is enduring. Her attribution concern nevertheless remains central: the long path from corrector concepts through practical implementation and instrument development makes the precise laureate boundary harder to establish than it is for B001. Optical lattice clocks are likewise a durable enabling instrument, but their intended prize-worthy contribution can be stated more narrowly and credited more cleanly."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "Lindroth regards B013 as a mature and predictive theoretical account of high-harmonic generation, provided its recollision mechanism and quantum theory can be separated from the 2023 attosecond-methods recognition.",
        "response": "The recollision framework is a major physical insight with extensive experimental validation. I remain reluctant to prefer it until the boundary from the recent attosecond recognition is demonstrably clear and the relation of the proposed theorists to experimental originators is resolved. B001 does not require such a difficult distinction from an already recognized achievement, and its experimental reproducibility and exact citation are presently firmer."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record supports limiting credit to Katori and Ye for the lattice-clock achievement while appropriately distinguishing later optical-clock development.",
      "Whether the citation can remain sufficiently precise to avoid implying that a redefinition of the second or all applications of optical clocks are already attributable to this award.",
      "Whether the attribution boundaries for B011 and B062 can be resolved strongly enough to alter their standing as alternatives."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No candidate-specific conflict is apparent from the supplied profile. My WACQT connection overlaps institutionally with Göran Johansson, but the supplied evidence identifies no relevant collaboration or financial connection to B001 or its proposed laureates."
  }
}
